    "sample_id": "helpsteer3:train:7cfb50f4dabc04f271d12f4fc6e800f64b164ba6b0f8b5af27364a8175fbb830",
    "task": "Write dialogue from a scene from the animated teen “Jane”, where 14 year old Jane, Jane’s 14 year old girlfriend Sam, Jane’s 14 year old friend and neighbour Aaron Ling and Aaron’s 12 year old sister Molly-Rose Ling hanging out at school when every single student at the school has to go to the school auditorium to hear an important announcement, there is a new student coming to the school (a girl similar in personality with Violet Beauregarde from “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory”, but make sure in the dialogue Violet Beauregarde from “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory” isn’t mentioned)",
    "chosen": " INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY\n\n*Jane, Sam, Aaron, and Molly-Rose are standing by their lockers, chatting.*\n\nJANE: (leaning against her locker) I can't believe we have to go to the auditorium again. I hope it's not another lecture on how to wash our hands.\n\nSAM: (smirking) Maybe it's just a ploy to make us miss math class.\n\nAARON: (shrugging) I don't mind. Anything to get out of Mr. Thompson's droning.\n\nMOLLY-ROSE: (excitedly) Maybe it's something fun! Like a magic show or a puppet theater!\n\n*Jane chuckles and ruffles Molly-Rose's hair.*\n\nJANE: I doubt it, Molly. But you never know.\n\n*The intercom crackles to life, and the PRINCIPAL's voice echoes through the hallway.*\n\nPRINCIPAL: (over intercom) Attention all students, please make your way to the auditorium immediately for an important announcement.\n\n*The four of them start walking towards the auditorium, blending into the crowd of students.*\n\nSAM: (curiously) What do you think it's about this time?\n\nAARON: (speculating) Maybe they're finally going to fix the vending machines.\n\nJANE: (skeptical) Or maybe they're just going to tell us they're out of order forever.\n\n*They enter the auditorium and find seats together.*\n\nMOLLY-ROSE: (pointing to the stage) Look, there's a microphone. Maybe it's a concert!\n\n*The principal walks onto the stage, followed by a girl with a confident, almost arrogant, stride. She has a competitive gleam in her eyes.*\n\nPRINCIPAL: (smiling) Thank you all for coming. We have a special announcement today. We have a new student joining us. Please welcome, Genevieve Hartley.\n\n*Genevieve steps up to the microphone, her voice oozing with self-assurance.*\n\nGENEVIEVE: (smiling smugly) Hello, everyone. I'm Genevieve, and I'm thrilled to be here. I've heard so much about this school, and I can't wait to show you all what I'm made of. I'm sure we're going to have a... (pauses, smirks) ...competitive time together.\n\n*Jane, Sam, Aaron, and Molly-Rose exchange glances, each raising an eyebrow at Genevieve's introduction.*\n\nJANE: (whispering) Well, this should be interesting.\n\n*They all settle in, ready to see what this new dynamic will bring to their school.*",
    "rejected": "INT. SCHOOL AUDITORIUM - DAY\n\nThe school auditorium is filled with students, buzzing with anticipation. Jane, Sam, Aaron, and Molly-Rose are standing together, whispering excitedly.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nI can't believe it. A new student!\n\nSAM\n(whispering)\nYeah, I heard she's really cool.\n\nAaron looks at Jane and Sam, a bit confused.\n\nAARON\n(whispering)\nWhat's so cool about a new student?\n\nMolly-Rose giggles, looking at Aaron.\n\nMOLLY-ROSE\n(whispering)\nMaybe she's like Violet Beauregarde.\n\nJane and Sam exchange a puzzled look.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nViolet Beauregarde? Who's that?\n\nSam rolls her eyes, trying to explain.\n\nSAM\n(whispering)\nOh, she's from that movie, \"Charlie and the Chocolate Factory.\"\n\nAaron looks at Sam, intrigued.\n\nAARON\n(whispering)\nWhat's that about?\n\nSAM\n(whispering)\nIt's a movie about a chocolate factory and a girl who can blow up like a balloon.\n\nMolly-Rose looks at Jane, excitedly.\n\nMOLLY-ROSE\n(whispering)\nMaybe she'll blow up in our school!\n\nJane and Sam laugh, trying to calm Molly-Rose down.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nNo, Molly-Rose, she's just a character in a movie.\n\nAaron looks at Jane, still curious.\n\nAARON\n(whispering)\nWhy would she be like that?\n\nSAM\n(whispering)\nIt's just a fictional story. She's not real.\n\nMolly-Rose looks disappointed, but Jane tries to cheer her up.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nHey, maybe she'll be a great friend to us!\n\nThe auditorium doors open, and the new student walks in. She's a girl with a bright smile and a confident stride.\n\nNEW STUDENT\n(whispering)\nHi, I'm Emily. Nice to meet you all.\n\nThe students look at Emily, intrigued by her confidence.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nWow, she's really cool.\n\nSAM\n(whispering)\nYeah, she's definitely different from the other students.\n\nAaron looks at Emily, impressed.\n\nAARON\n(whispering)\nShe seems really smart.\n\nMolly-Rose looks at Emily, excitedly.\n\nMOLLY-ROSE\n(whispering)\nMaybe she'll be like Violet Beauregarde!\n\nJane and Sam laugh, trying to calm Molly-Rose down.\n\nJANE\n(whispering)\nNo, Molly-Rose, she's just a person.\n\nThe principal announces that Emily will be joining their class. The students cheer, excited to meet their new classmate.\n\nFADE OUT.",
