          "score": 3,
          "reasoning": "@Response 2 is much better than @Response 1. It is able to fulfill all of the prompt's requests without any issues, while @Response 1 incorrectly mentioned Violet Beauregarde several times, the new student did not reflect her personality, and there was no introductory scene before the students entered the auditorium.",
          "feedback1": "The response is slightly helpful. It does not fulfill most of the prompt's requirements. For instance, the scene immediately begins in the auditorium, when it wasn't supposed to since there is no scene of the students going to the auditorium or hearing an announcement. The response also mentions Violet Beauregarde, which it also wasn't supposed to do. The lines by some of the characters have a similar structure throughout, making the response somewhat repetitive. It also doesn't make sense that the characters would react to Violet in a positive manner, when her personality is arrogant and condescending. Because of these issues, the response is poor and only slightly helpful.",
          "feedback2": "The response is perfectly helpful. It includes everything that the prompt asked for without any issues. It even manages to recognize that the new student is of an arrogant and competitive nature, which reflects the personality of Violet Beauregarde very well. The response is of an ideal length and does not have any contradictions whatsoever. There is not much that can be done to improve the response in its current state."
        },
        {
          "score": 3,
          "reasoning": "@Response 2 is much better than @Response 1. @Response 2 includes the prompt's request to not directly mention Violet, while @Response 1 does not. ",
          "feedback1": "The response is not helpful. The response does not listen to the prompt's requests. The prompt specifically asks to not mention Violet Beauregarde and Charlie and the Chocolate Factory, yet the response mentions this character twice. There is also a lack of plot advancement. The conversation has repetitions and no resolution. ",
          "feedback2": "The response is perfectly helpful. The response mentions the way that the new student is acting. The new student is acting smug and competitive, which is very similar to Violet Beauregarde. The fact that the new student's personality is similar to Violet's personality matches the prompt's request to have similarities without directly mentioning Violet. "
        },
        {
          "score": 3,
          "reasoning": "@Response 2 is much better than @Response 1. While both prompts follow the plot line given by the prompt, @Response 1 violates the requirement of omitting anything about Violet Beauregarde or Charlie and the Chocolate Factory. ",
          "feedback1": "The response is slightly helpful. While the plot line and characters are what was asked for, there is a major issue with the prompt requirement. The prompt specifically stated that \"Violet Beauregarde\" and \"Charlie and the Chocolate Factory\" are not to be mentioned in the dialogue yet they are prevalent throughout it. ",
          "feedback2": "The response is mostly helpful. As the group walks to the auditorium, they speculate about what it will be about. The principal announces to go to the auditorium, and as they walk, they speculate again. This continued speculation seems repetitive. When they enter the auditorium and see the microphone, the speculation afterward is warranted, and it is fine to include new information as it is given. Other than this, the response perfectly encapsulates the character of Violet Beauregarde without mentioning her or Charlie and the Chocolate Factory as the prompt requested. "
